      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.661,
          "end": 8.142,
          "en": "Now with all these bindings, you hopefully got an overview of how you can work with Svelte",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 8.142,
          "end": 12.606,
          "en": "and its bindings to conveniently get access to form values. And using two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 12.622,
          "end": 16.99,
          "en": "here really is extremely helpful, and you'll often use it when working with forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 18.098,
          "end": 23.51,
          "en": "There is another way of getting access to any element on the page though, so besides using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 23.703,
          "end": 26.899,
          "en": "two-way binding, and also not limited to inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 27.736,
          "end": 31.36,
          "en": "Let me first demonstrate it with the help of an input though. Let's say here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 31.36,
          "end": 32.197,
          "en": "we have an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 32.713,
          "end": 36.489,
          "en": "and we have a button, and I only need the value once I clicked that button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 37.361,
          "end": 41.726,
          "en": "So here in on:click, I'll",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 41.759,
          "end": 47.017,
          "en": "trigger saveData, which is a function I have yet to add. So let's do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 47.017,
          "end": 48.867,
          "en": "that quickly. Here we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 50.372,
          "end": 55.405,
          "en": "saveData, and I'm not accepting any event object in here because that would be my",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 55.68,
          "end": 59.282,
          "en": "click event and I'm not interested in that. But I do want to get the text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 59.347,
          "end": 60.326,
          "en": "that was entered into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 60.39,
          "end": 66.857,
          "en": "this input. Of course, we could set up two-way binding with bind:value and then storing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 66.889,
          "end": 71.591,
          "en": "data which is in that input in some variable. But if I only need this in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 71.688,
          "end": 73.325,
          "en": "a read-only way and I never",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 73.325,
          "end": 76.486,
          "en": "set the value anywhere else, I could do it and it would not be wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 76.919,
          "end": 78.027,
          "en": "And in most cases, you will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 78.123,
          "end": 84.029,
          "en": "probably do it with two-way binding, but you can actually also simply read the value from the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 84.632,
          "end": 90.839,
          "en": "So of course what we could do here is we could console.log document.querySelector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 91.853,
          "end": 96.168,
          "en": "and then maybe give this, uh, some ID username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
