        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 120.069,
          "end": 122.619,
          "en": "This is not the Svelte-ish way of doing it though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 123.341,
          "end": 126.628,
          "en": "This is vanilla JavaScript code which you can use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 127.029,
          "end": 128.44,
          "en": "but there is a more elegant solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 128.697,
          "end": 131.487,
          "en": "And you might remember that I used a similar approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 131.616,
          "end": 134.085,
          "en": "earlier in the course where I also used querySelector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 134.085,
          "end": 136.699,
          "en": "because I had no better tool for the job.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 137.613,
          "end": 139.153,
          "en": "Now actually, there is a better tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 139.922,
          "end": 142.632,
          "en": "You can use binding, but a special form of binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 143.209,
          "end": 146.192,
          "en": "So instead of relying on selecting this by ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 147.635,
          "end": 148.982,
          "en": "you can instead add bind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 148.998,
          "end": 150.65,
          "en": "but now you don't bind to value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 150.762,
          "end": 153.504,
          "en": "because I don't want two-way binding, but to this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 153.969,
          "end": 157.112,
          "en": "which is simply a special syntax understood by Svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 157.256,
          "end": 160.447,
          "en": "This, this thing here is not a normal attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 160.688,
          "end": 161.666,
          "en": "you could add to an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 161.89,
          "end": 164.039,
          "en": "This is simply understood by the Svelte compiler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 164.552,
          "end": 165.788,
          "en": "And by binding to this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 166.237,
          "end": 169.8,
          "en": "you can store a reference to that element here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 169.929,
          "end": 173.026,
          "en": "a pointer to that element in a variable of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 174.005,
          "end": 175.594,
          "en": "So now we can add a new variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 176.332,
          "end": 177.985,
          "en": "usernameInput, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 178.98,
          "end": 182.864,
          "en": "And this is the variable which I'll use down there, usernameInput.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 183.651,
          "end": 186.379,
          "en": "So now a pointer at this HTML element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 186.459,
          "end": 189.091,
          "en": "or at this DOM element to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.493,
          "end": 191.402,
          "en": "is stored in usernameInput.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 192.397,
          "end": 194.306,
          "en": "And therefore here in saveData,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 194.819,
          "end": 198.894,
          "en": "I can now console.log usernameInput.value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.894,
          "end": 201.397,
          "en": "because this points at this HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.942,
          "end": 205.119,
          "en": "And hence now if I enter super here and I click save,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 206.033,
          "end": 207.124,
          "en": "you see that still works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 207.557,
          "end": 208.889,
          "en": "But of course that's way shorter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.162,
          "end": 211.328,
          "en": "than manually selecting this with querySelector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.809,
          "end": 214.119,
          "en": "And we also don't have to add the ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.135,
          "end": 215.082,
          "en": "we can remove that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 215.258,
          "end": 217.617,
          "en": "because now this reference and connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 217.971,
          "end": 219.64,
          "en": "is set up behind the scenes by Svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 220.315,
          "end": 221.615,
          "en": "Now, this is not two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.84,
          "end": 224.056,
          "en": "This is really just a pointer at the full element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.409,
          "end": 226.464,
          "en": "We're not restricted to reading its value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.721,
          "end": 227.716,
          "en": "We can do whatever we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.085,
          "end": 231.008,
          "en": "We can manipulate it, though I would not recommend that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.297,
          "end": 233.32,
          "en": "You shouldn't change it programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.625,
          "end": 236.643,
          "en": "You should always change your DOM through Svelte",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.691,
          "end": 238.232,
          "en": "by the instructions you place down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.859,
          "end": 240.801,
          "en": "But you can read any data you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 241.187,
          "end": 243.37,
          "en": "You can check out the CSS classes on the element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.515,
          "end": 246.068,
          "en": "You can do whatever you want because if we log it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.084,
          "end": 248.028,
          "en": "you'll see it's just the full element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.43,
          "end": 252.43,
          "en": "So if I console.log this here and I press save again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.607,
          "end": 253.603,
          "en": "it's the full input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.101,
          "end": 257.924,
          "en": "By the way, if you want to inspect it here, you can use console.dir, and now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.053,
          "end": 260.688,
          "en": "you get an inspectable JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.848,
          "end": 268.415,
          "en": "object. So this is really the full DOM element, and this does not just work with HTML input elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.672,
          "end": 274.529,
          "en": "it works with any HTML element and your own components as well. So we can also use a div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.529,
          "end": 281.821,
          "en": "instead and bind this to someDiv, which of course is a variable I have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 281.934,
          "end": 283.264,
          "en": "yet to add. So here is someDiv.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 285.614,
          "end": 291.403,
          "en": "And now for simplicity, when we click Save Data, I can now also console.dir someDiv.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 294.532,
          "end": 298.465,
          "en": "So it's the same button as before, but now I'm binding this here, this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 298.594,
          "end": 299.716,
          "en": "div, to the someDiv",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 300.583,
          "end": 305.716,
          "en": "variable, and therefore I can now interact with the div and inspect it and do whatever I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 305.876,
          "end": 310.608,
          "en": "Again, changing something there is not recommended. You should always do that with the help of Svelte's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 310.768,
          "end": 314.682,
          "en": "normal syntax, but reading values from it can be really useful.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
